    "title": "Ohio man charged in death of 5 month old girl - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Adam Conn Daniel Griffin ,\n18 hours ago\nCOLUMBUS, Ohio (WCMH) — A man is facing a murder charge after a 5-month-old girl died Monday on the far southeast side of the city.\nAccording to Columbus police, Madison Township medics responded to a call for a child who was having difficulty breathing on the 400 block of Willard Brook Road, just north of Canal Winchester, approximately 10:50 a.m. Monday.\nThe girl was taken to the hospital in critical condition. During the examination of the child, doctors said her injuries were inconsistent with what police were told. The girl died at 6:32 p.m. due to “severe blunt force trauma to the head,” according to court records.\nGlenn McIntosh, 32, was in charge of the infant’s care at the time of her injuries, police said, and was reportedly alone with her in the White Ash home. He has been charged with murder and is being held in Franklin County Jail.\nMcIntosh is scheduled for an arraignment hearing at 9 a.m. Wednesday.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WKBN.com.",
